  <title>Flash messages</title>
  <p>
    Flash messages are temporary messages on the braille display that provide feedback from
    Orca, such as confirmation that a setting has changed. They replace the displayed content
    without moving focus or the caret. When a message expires, Orca restores the previous
    display contents.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-flash-messages">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>Flash Messages</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Flash messages</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca shows messages and command feedback in braille. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Messages are detailed</gui>: Chooses detailed
          rather than brief messages when both forms are available. For example, detailed
          feedback can include a setting's name and its new value, while brief feedback gives
          just the value. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Messages are persistent</gui>: Keeps a flash
          message displayed until another update replaces it, instead of restoring the previous
          contents after a timeout. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Duration (secs):</gui> Sets how long
          temporary braille messages are displayed when they are not persistent. This setting is
          ignored when messages are persistent. Default: 5 seconds. Range: 1 to 100.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
